damaged_code:
```rust
// Too early: client CPU work counted as network/server latency
let start = Instant::now();
let json_bytes = serde_json::to_vec(&large_struct)?;
socket.write_all(&json_bytes)?;
socket.read_exact(&mut buf)?;
let latency = start.elapsed();

// Too late: time blocked in write_all / send-buffer queueing excluded
socket.write_all(&payload)?;
let start = Instant::now();
socket.read_exact(&mut buf)?;
let latency = start.elapsed();
```

fix:
Prepare the request buffer first, take the start timestamp immediately before the write/send call, and stop it when the response is received. In an open-loop load generator, start from the request's intended send time instead, which precedes the write.
```rust
let json_bytes = serde_json::to_vec(&large_struct)?;
let start = Instant::now();
socket.write_all(&json_bytes)?;
socket.read_exact(&mut buf)?;
hist.record(start.elapsed().as_nanos() as u64)?;
```
